@page
@model WorkLedger.Pages.PersistenceModel

<section>
    <h1>Persistence wiring</h1>
    <p>
        The EF Core implementation stores work items in `workledger.db` via `WorkLedgerDbContext`.
        The context is registered in <code>Program.cs</code> and the app ensures the SQLite file is created at startup.
    </p>
    <pre><code>builder.Services.AddDbContext&lt;WorkLedgerDbContext&gt;(options =>
    options.UseSqlite("Data Source=workledger.db"));
builder.Services.AddScoped&lt;IWorkItemRepository, EfWorkItemRepository&gt;();</code></pre>
    <p>
        `EfWorkItemRepository` saves, updates, and deletes items by calling <code>SaveChanges()</code> after each mutation.
        The service layer never needs to care whether the repository is backed by memory or a database.
    </p>
</section>
